id: pm-github-generated-sync-artifacts
title: Publish declared generated artifacts with gated tracker changes
description: "Track https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/255 and the stale self-host bundle reported in https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/issues/228."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog-unreleased,"gh:unbraind/pm-github#255"
created_at: "2026-11-25T08:32:37.193Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-25T09:54:35.622Z"
deadline: "2026-11-27T08:32:37.193Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A declared repository-root artifact regenerated by the caller npm script ships with the tracker in one privacy-gated commit. Undeclared changes and workflow paths are refused.
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-25T08:36:06.084Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced on the unmodified workflow with a real tracker, bare remote, and a source bundle verified from committed HEAD. The self-host hook regenerates the file, then scope rejects selfhost.bundle, including when the declaration is supplied. Without regeneration the sync publishes and the fixture acceptance reports a stale bundle. Baseline receipt: 2 passed, 1 failed. pm-vcs write mode reads indexed path names and working-tree bytes, so the same commit can contain both outputs if the tracker is staged before generation. The reusable closeout workflow has the same publication boundary."
  "2026-11-25T08:41:12.923Z",codex-agent,"Implementation uses the existing post-import and post-closeout npm script inputs plus the new generated-paths input. Declared outputs are checked against HEAD before the hook, scoped as literal root files, and included in the final privacy scan and committed-tree comparison. New tracker files are indexed before generation. Tracker-only checks still control publication and no-op behavior. Neither extension commands nor JSON or TOON schemas need a new option."
  "2026-11-25T08:53:07.024Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy, with tests and unaffected workflow logic held fixed. Restoring the original path matcher failed both declared publication tests. Bypassing the out-of-scope refusal failed both undeclared-output tests. Removing literal root-name validation failed both protected workflow path tests. Omitting generated files from the privacy diff failed the credential rejection test. Omitting the raw output from the policy snapshot failed the late-write test. Bypassing the clean-output check failed the dirty-path and two non-Git tests. Removing the tracker no-op guard failed the repeat-sync assertion. Each mutation returned exit 1. The pm-vcs rollout is tracked by https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/issues/228 and needs a caller wrapper that regenerates the changelog before self-host:write."
  "2026-11-25T09:12:00.780Z",codex-agent,"The broader Node 22 run caught a standalone workflow diagnostic with no resolved tracker and a stale literal in the existing closeout no-op mutation test. The diagnostic helper now loads independently, and the original mutation test still removes the same tracker-only guard. The corrected focused run passed 14 of 14, and the original no-op behavior and mutation passed 2 of 2. Removing only the diagnostic initialization guard failed the existing reporter test with an unbound variable. After restoring the guard that test passed. Bun focused regressions passed 13 of 13 and the package metadata and packed runtime smoke passed 8 of 8. The PM-linked isolated test command passed 1 of 1 and reported 10 tests."
  "2026-11-25T09:32:50.971Z",codex-agent,"Local verification complete. Node 22.18 quick depth ran 748 tests across 26 changed or referencing files, with 746 initial passes and only the two corrected compatibility assertions failing initially. The corrected focused and no-op reruns passed 14 of 14 and 2 of 2. The four late and undeclared legacy scope tests passed at full selection. Both corrected compatibility cases passed on Bun as well. Packed npm and Bun diagnostics passed for JSON and TOON. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint and docstring gates passed. Strict PM health passed with an isolated global tracker after the shared environment reported an unrelated extension version mismatch. Coverage and full release gates are CI-owned."
  "2026-11-25T09:54:34.391Z",codex-agent,"The first exact-head CI run at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/45586647836 reported 2136 of 2141 Node 22 tests passing. The five failures came from stale ownership-inventory line anchors and the attestation scanner rejecting the Bash array-length expression. The Node 26 release job reached the same attestation test failure. Both workflows now test whether the first parsed name exists, and the repository generator refreshed the inventory. Node 22 reruns passed 45 inventory, attestation and related tests and 14 workflow fixtures. The added PM-linked gate passed its 13 tests. Reverting only the old predicates in a disposable Git checkout caused four attestation findings, and reverting only the generated inventory failed its check. Both gates passed again after restoration."
